## TEST CASE 1d
This test should be run with .ts as a command-line argument.

This tests the behavior of the program when it is given a valid command-line argument, but
for a file that is not listed in the directory.

A successful test result should just be a context file that contains the directory structure and
no additional text.

**Command:**
```bash
get_context case1 .ts
```

**Console output:**
```bash
Generating context file for directory /Users/aiden/Code/personal/get_context/test_suite
Reading only files with extensions ['.ts']
Generated 'context.txt' at '/Users/aiden/Code/personal/get_context/test_suite/context.txt'
```

**context.txt output:**
```
Directory Structure:
case1/
	DESCRIPTION
	case1-0.txt
	case1-1.py
	case1_sub0/
		case1_sub0-0.txt
		case1_sub0-1.java
