			case1_sub_0_sub0-2.py
	case1_sub1/
		case1_sub1-0.txt
		case1_sub1-1.js

==================================================
```

# ERROR CASES
The following test cases should NOT result in successful output. These tests demonstrate how the
program handles errors or undefined inputs under various conditions.

## ERROR CASE 1a
This test case should be run with no command line arguments.

This should result in the program displaying the usage guide to the user. The context.txt file
should not be generated.

**Command:**
```bash
get_context
```

**Console output:**
```bash
Error: Invalid CLI arguments
Usage:
  python3 -m get_context <directory> [file_extensions...]
Description:
  This program processes all human-readable files in the given directory and its subdirectories.
  Optionally, you can specify file extensions to filter which files to include.
Examples:
  python3 -m get_context .         # Process all human-readable files.
  python3 -m get_context . .py .txt  # Process only .py and .txt files.
```